.TH "ROARK\-SIMULATION\-ENVIRONMENT\-UPDATE" "1" "" "roark-simulation-environment-update" "Roark Analytics API Manual"
.SH "NAME"
roark\-simulation\-environment\-update \- Update an environment
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark simulation environment update
\fIenvironment\-id\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Updates one of the project's environments. Only the fields sent are changed. Runs already built keep the snapshot they were built with. Roark\-curated environments cannot be edited (403).
.SH "API"
PUT /v1/simulation/environment/{environmentId}
.SH "ARGUMENTS"
.TP
\fIenvironment\-id\fR
The environment\-id.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<value>\fR
Display name, shown wherever a flow variant references the environment Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-description\fR \fI<value>\fR
Optional note on when to use this environment Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-background\-noise\fR \fI<value>\fR
The noise bed played underneath the simulated caller. NONE plays nothing. One of: NONE, AIRPORT, CHILDREN_PLAYING, CITY, COFFEE_SHOP, CONSTRUCTION, CRYING_BABY, DRIVING, LIBRARY, OFFICE, THUNDERSTORM, TRAIN. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-background\-noise\-volume\fR \fI<value>\fR
How loud the bed plays, as a gain from 0 (silent) to 1 (as loud as the caller). Defaults to 0.1, which sits well under the caller. Ignored on Vapi endpoints, which have no level control. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-line\-quality\fR \fI<value>\fR
The phone line the simulated caller is on: packet loss applied to its 20 ms audio packets, per direction. The loss pattern is seeded per call, so a redial loses the same packets. CLEAR: No loss. MINOR_LOSS: 1% random, both ways. CELL_EDGE: 5% in 80 ms gaps, both ways. POOR_CONNECTION: 10% in 120 ms gaps, both ways. ONE_WAY_DEGRADED: 8% in 80 ms gaps, toward the agent only. CUSTOM: the per\-direction loss in `lineCustom`, up to 20% in 0.5 steps, with a mean burst of up to 10 packets (omit it for random loss). Defaults to CLEAR. One of: CLEAR, MINOR_LOSS, CELL_EDGE, POOR_CONNECTION, ONE_WAY_DEGRADED, CUSTOM. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-line\-custom\fR \fI<value>\fR
The per\-direction loss of a CUSTOM line. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-line\-custom.to\-agent\fR \fI<value>\fR
The caller's audio on its way to the agent: what the agent hears. Omit for no loss. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-line\-custom.from\-agent\fR \fI<value>\fR
The agent's audio on its way to the caller: what the caller hears. Omit for no loss. Optional.
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-data\fR \fI<json>\fR
Request body as JSON, or @file to read one (@\- for stdin).
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-input\fR
